TI  - A Case of Pulmonary Nodular Schistosomiasis.
PG  - 104-108
AB  - Bilharzia is a parasitic infection particularly affecting the digestive tract and 
      urinary tract. Lung involvement is rarely reported. We report a case of pulmonary 
      bilharzioma of nodular type surrounded by ground glass opacities diagnosed on 
      CT-scan and associated with a hepatic nodule, in a 41-year-old woman. The 
      disappearance of the pulmonary nodule under antischistosomal treatment made it 
      possible to make the diagnosis a posteriori without going through an invasive 
      process.
