TI  - NRITLD Protocol for the Management of Outpatient Cases of COVID-19.
PG  - 192-196
AB  - Despite the fact that about two years have passed since the onset of the COVID-19 
      pandemic, there is still no curative treatment for the disease. Most cases of 
      COVID-19 have mild or moderate illness and do not require hospitalization. This 
      guideline released by the National Research Institute of Tuberculosis and Lung 
      Diseases (NRITLD), Masih Daneshvari Hospital COVID-19 Expert Group to provide a 
      treatment guide for outpatient management of COVID-19.
