TI  - Thoracotomy for Extracting Grass Inflorescence Aspiration: a Case Report.
PG  - 79-81
AB  - Following aspiration of grass inflorescence, it often migrates to the peripheral 
      part of the airway due to its unique shape. It often causes complications like 
      chronic pneumonia, recurrent asthmatic attacks, lung abscess, recurrent 
      hemoptysis, and bronchiectasis that may necessitate surgical intervention. In 
      this case, we have reported a 13-year-old boy with grass inflorescence 
      aspiration. The bronchoscopic procedure failed to remove the foreign body, so he 
      underwent thoracotomy.
