TI  - Pulmonary Thromboembolism Following Spine Surgery: Clinical Suspicion is the Key.
PG  - 184-187
AB  - Pulmonary thromboembolism following spine surgery, although rare, could end into 
      devastating outcome. Gold standard for it diagnosis is pulmonary CT angiography 
      but in operating theatre, clinical suspicion is the key to diagnose. Here we 
      report a case of pulmonary embolism with classic clinical findings which approved 
      using pulmonary CT angiography and echocardiography.
