TI  - Treatment of Esophageal Perforation with Primary Closure and Reinforcement Using 
      TachoSil.
PG  - 84-87
AB  - Two patients with iatrogenic esophageal perforation following rigid esophagoscopy 
      for foreign body removal were successfully treated with primary repair and 
      reinforcement using a collagen patch coated with human fibrinogen and thrombin 
      (TachoSil, Nycomed, Austria, Vienna). The clinical implication of this report is 
      that TachoSil can be used to bolster the repair site of esophageal perforation.
