TI  - Health Care Associated Middle East Respiratory Syndrome (MERS): A Case from Iran.
PG  - 262-7
AB  - Middle East respiratory syndrome coronavirus (MERS-CoV) Infection, has caused 
      recurrent outbreaks worldwide. It is associated with severe morbidity and 
      mortality, and is not treatable with the currently available antiviral therapies. 
      We present a case of a 43 year-old male healthcare provider, who admitted with 
      productive cough, dyspnea, myalgia, pleuritic chest pain and fever. Computed 
      tomography (CT) showed bilateral ground glass opacities and consolidation. Sputum 
      polymerase chain reaction (PCR) for MERS-coronavirus was positive.
