TI  - Isolated traumatic bilateral first rib fracture: a rare entity.
PG  - 60-3
AB  - Since the first rib is protected very well by the overlying soft tissue and 
      bones, its fracture is a major injury and a considerable force is required to do 
      it. Therefore, an isolated fracture of this rib is unusual. A 28-year-old healthy 
      female had an accident while crossing the road and a heavy object fell on her. 
      She had severe pain behind her clavicle region and was immediately hospitalized 
      and examined. Thorough clinical examination and different relevant investigations 
      surprisingly disclosed isolated bilateral first rib fracture which is a very rare 
      clinical condition.
