VI  - 12
IP  - 4
DP  - 2013
TI  - Spontaneous esophageal perforation presenting as a right-sided pleural effusion: 
      a case report.
PG  - 53-7
AB  - Spontaneous esophageal perforation or Boerhaave's syndrome is an uncommon 
      condition that may occur following forceful vomiting and lead to mediastinitis. 
      It is associated with high mortality and morbidity in absence of therapy. We 
      present a case of spontaneous esophageal perforation in a 63 year-old man who 
      developed a right-sided effusion, an unusual presentation. This case report and 
      the relevant literature reveal that delay in prompt surgical repair is associated 
      with a high morbidity and mortality.
