DP  - 2014
TI  - Thoracoscopic lobectomy in a patient with permanent tracheostomy.
PG  - 52-4
AB  - One Lung Ventilation (OLV) is the preferred method of anesthesia in the vast 
      majority of thoracic operations, especially thoracoscopic procedures. Although 
      double lumen endotracheal tubes are usually used to conduct OLV during thoracic 
      operations, in patients with permanent tracheostomy, because of short trachea, 
      keeping these tubes safe in place is usually difficult. Thus, OLV in patients 
      with permanent tracheostomy may be challenging or even impossible. Herein, we 
      report a patient with permanent tracheostomy who underwent successful OLV and 
      thoracoscopic lobectomy.
