VI  - 10
IP  - 3
DP  - 2011
TI  - A 38-year-old woman with scimitar syndrome.
PG  - 63-6
AB  - Scimitar syndrome is a rare clinical syndrome which consists of anomalous right 
      pulmonary venous return to the inferior vena cava. Scimitar syndrome classically 
      involves the right lung and is most commonly reported in very early infancy. 
      However, it is occasionally seen in adults. We present a 38 year-old woman 
      complaining of dry cough and exertional dyspnea during moderate exercise with 
      right lung scimitar syndrome. The chest radiography showed increased radiolucency 
      of the left lung and heart dextroposition with a characteristic appearance of 
      scimitar sign which is a curvilinear density in the right middle and lower 
      pulmonary fields resembling a curved Turkish sword.
