TI  - Different and Unpredictable Clinical Outcome of Ruptured Pulmonary Hydatid Cysts.
PG  - 217-21
AB  - Most authors believe that the best treatment for pulmonary hydatid disease is 
      surgical evacuation. Although albendazole has been used prophylactically before 
      surgery, there are many reports about increased incidence of the rupture of cyst 
      after albendazole therapy, which can cause some complications. In this case 
      report we present a patient with bilateral pulmonary hydatid cyst that was 
      ruptured after using albendazole and different strategies were used for 
      management of each cyst.
