TI  - Treatment Considerations of Lung Involvement in Rheumatologic Disease.
PG  - 265-74
LID - 10.1159/000441238 [doi]
AB  - Lung involvement in rheumatologic diseases has a broad spectrum of clinical and 
      radiological presentations, from acute and inflammatory predominance to chronic 
      and fibrotic lung disorders. Therapy has to be guided by the type of 
      rheumatologic disease, the kind of lung involvement and the risk associated with 
      the clinical state of the patient and prognostic factors. Although several 
      therapeutic approaches have been used, the best treatment is still not certain; 
      clinical trials are mandatory, which would require a better knowledge of the 
      pulmonary pathogenesis of immunologic diseases. The following review is focused 
      on the therapeutic options for those rheumatologic disorders that could present 
      as a predominant interstitial lung disease which may confer a bad or 
      life-threatening prognosis.
