TI  - The Solitary Pulmonary Nodule.
PG  - 160-72
LID - 10.1159/000430996 [doi]
AB  - Due to the high etiological diversity and the potential for malignancy, pulmonary 
      nodules represent a clinical challenge, becoming increasingly frequent as the 
      number of CT examinations rises. The topic gains even more importance as clear 
      evidence for the effectiveness of CT screening was provided by the National Lung 
      Screening Trial (NLST). Yet, the results were tempered by the high false-positive 
      rate and the requirement of performing further diagnostic procedures. The 
      management of those detected solitary pulmonary nodules is currently based on the 
      individuals' risk of developing lung cancer, the pulmonary nodule characteristics 
      and the capability of diagnostic and therapeutic approaches.
