TI  - Primary amyloidosis involving mediastinal lymph nodes: diagnosis by 
      transbronchial needle aspiration.
PG  - 218-20
AB  - Amyloidosis is an uncommon disease caused by the deposition of abnormal proteins 
      within soft tissues. Pulmonary and mediastinal lymph node involvement of the 
      disease is rare. When mediastinal lymph nodes are affected, the diagnostic 
      approach should include sample collection for pathological examination. 
      Transbronchial fine needle aspiration is a useful and safe procedure for sampling 
      mediastinal lymph nodes. This paper describes the first case of amyloidosis that 
      involves mediastinal lymph nodes diagnosed by transbronchial needle aspiration.
