TI  - Rhabdomyolysis after the administration of itraconazole to an asthmatic patient 
      with bronchopulmonary aspergillosis.
PG  - 289-91
AB  - It is known that the coadministration of itraconazole with cholesterol-lowering 
      statins may induce muscle damage. We describe the case of a patient with 
      steroid-dependent asthma, steroid-induced severe myopathy and allergic 
      bronchopulmonary aspergillosis who developed rhabdomyolysis and acute renal 
      failure following a approximately 6-week treatment with itraconazole, even 
      without the concomitant use of HMG-CoA reductase inhibitors.
