TI  - Pathogenesis and treatment of primary spontaneous pneumothorax: an overview.
PG  - 431-8
AB  - The exact pathogenesis of primary spontaneous pneumothorax (PSP) remains unknown. 
      Furthermore, various specialists including pulmonologists, surgeons, emergency 
      care physicians, radiologists and others are known to treat this disorder in 
      clinical practice. As a consequence, guidelines on the management of PSP are 
      scarce, and differences in treatment approaches persist. In this paper, evidence 
      on the pathogenesis and on various treatment techniques and strategies is 
      reviewed. An algorithmic treatment approach is proposed.
