TI  - Two cases of 'asthma' revealing a diverticulum of Kommerell.
PG  - 456-60
AB  - Among embryonic aortic vascular malformations, persistence of a right aortic arch 
      and aberrant left subclavian artery associated with a diverticulum of Kommerell 
      is rare, and is estimated to occur in 0.1% of the general population. We report 
      two cases of diverticulum of Kommerell in which tracheal compression due to the 
      vascular ring induced respiratory symptoms such as asthmatic dyspnoea. This 
      reminds us that at least a chest X-ray should be performed in newly diagnosed 
      asthmatic patients, focusing on the trachea and upper mediastinum. In case of 
      vascular abnormality, angiography and magnetic resonance are the best 
      investigations to define the abnormal anatomy and guide surgery.
