TI  - Intermittent positive airway pressure by nasal mask as a treatment for 
      respiratory insufficiency in a patient with syringomyelia.
PG  - 169-74
AB  - We report a case of a 73-year-old woman with chronic respiratory failure in 
      association with syringohydromyelia and sleep apnea. She was initially intubated 
      and mechanically ventilated. Weaning from the ventilator was only successful 
      after nasal intermittent positive airway pressure therapy was started. A 
      normalization of arterial blood gas exchange could be achieved.
