TI  - Massive pleural effusion as the presenting feature of a subarachnoid-pleural 
      fistula.
PG  - 96-9
AB  - A 14-year-old boy presented with a large symptomatic transudative pleural 
      effusion 4 months after spinal surgery for kyphoscoliosis. Computed tomography 
      myelography confirmed a subarachnoid-pleural fistula (SPF) with a 
      pseudo-meningocele communicating with the left pleural space. A review of the 
      literature indicates this to be a rare finding. The possibility of SPF should be 
      entertained in patients who present with a pleural effusion following 
      transthoracic spinal surgeries.
