TI  - Aortobronchial fistula presenting as recurrent hemoptysis and successfully 
      treated with an endovascular stent graft.
PG  - 537-9
AB  - Aortobronchial fistula (ABF) (aortopulmonary fistula) may cause a massive fatal 
      hemoptysis. We have recently seen a patient with ABF presenting with recurrent, 
      massive hemoptysis. She was successfully treated with an endovascular stent 
      graft. The endovascular stent graft may provide an alternative treatment of in 
      patients considered to be poor surgical candidates.
