TI  - Bronchiolitis obliterans with organizing pneumonia associated with acute Coxiella 
      burnetii infection.
PG  - 425-7
AB  - We report the case of a 62-year-old man who developed bronchiolitis obliterans 
      with organizing pneumonia (BOOP) associated with acute Coxiella burnetii 
      infection. The diagnosis of BOOP was made by fiber-optic transbronchial biopsy. 
      Treatment with corticosteroids resulted in rapid clinical improvement and 
      complete resolution of airspace opacities. To the best of our knowledge, this is 
      the first well-documented case of BOOP associated with C. burnetii infection. 
      This case suggests that this infection might trigger the development of BOOP.
