TI  - Radicular involvement and medullary invasion from a malignant mesothelioma.
PG  - 106-8
AB  - We present the case of a 57-year-old patient who had worked at a fiber-cement 
      factory for 28 years. The patient developed an epithelioid-type pleural 
      mesothelioma 5 years after retiring, after he was diagnosed with asbestosis. Only 
      5 months after the diagnosis of mesothelioma, a medullar section appeared to be 
      totally invaded by a tumor in the medullar canal, thus causing paraplegia and 
      affecting the bladder and anal sphincters. The patient underwent radiotherapy and 
      chemotherapy, and achieved partial recovery, but died 9 months after the 
      diagnosis.
