DP  - 2000
TI  - Deciduoid pleural mesothelioma affecting a young female without prior asbestos 
      exposure.
PG  - 456-8
AB  - Pleural mesothelioma is commonly associated to asbestos exposure. A 40-year-old 
      woman is described who presented with shortness of breath. She had a smoking 
      history but no history of asbestos exposure. Chest radiography and computed 
      tomography showed a large tumour on the right lower lung. An open pleural biopsy 
      was performed. A metastatic adenocarcinoma of the pleura was primarily diagnosed. 
      The tumour progressed and after surgical excision an accurate histological and 
      immunohistochemical examination was performed. It revealed a pleural mesothelioma 
      with a deciduoid differentiation that has not been described before.
