TI  - Small cell lung carcinoma presenting as acute cardiovascular collapse due to 
      tumour cell embolisation.
PG  - 323-6
AB  - We present a case of small cell lung carcinoma causing acute cardiovascular 
      collapse due to pulmonary tumour emboli. Although pulmonary tumour emboli may 
      complicate a number of malignancies, this is rarely seen in cases of carcinoma of 
      the bronchus. Patients suffering with pulmonary tumour emboli often have previous 
      symptoms, and show progressive dyspnoea. To our knowledge there have been no 
      reports of tumour emboli presenting acutely without any previous history of 
      symptoms.
