TI  - Primary Tracheal Mucosa-Associated Lymphoid Tissue Lymphoma Treated with a 
      Water-Jet Hybrid Knife: A Case Report.
PG  - 168-172
LID - 10.1159/000494064 [doi]
AB  - Primary mucosa-associated lymphoid tissue (MALT) lymphoma of the trachea is very 
      rare and is easily misdiagnosed as a bronchogenic carcinoma or benign tracheal 
      tumor. Here, we report a clinical case where a new clinical approach involving a 
      water-jet hybrid knife was employed in the diagnosis and treatment of primary 
      tracheal MALT lymphoma.
