TI  - Can Large Hydatid Cysts Resolve with Medical Treatment Alone?
PG  - 428-431
AB  - A 66-year-old female from a rural area in South Africa presented with 
      non-life-threatening haemoptysis. Radiologic and serological investigations 
      attributed her symptoms to bilateral, large echinococcal cysts. She declined 
      surgery despite her lung physiologic parameters, which deemed her eligible. 
      Medical therapy with oral albendazole was initiated with excellent clinical and 
      radiologic response during a follow-up period of 18 months. To our knowledge, 
      this is one of the first reported cases in the literature that shows complete 
      resolution of bilateral large echinococcal cysts with medical treatment alone in 
      an adult patient.
