TI  - An unexpected cause of diffuse alveolar hemorrhage in a kidney transplant 
      patient.
PG  - 504-7
LID - 10.1159/000358566 [doi]
AB  - Diffuse alveolar hemorrhage (DAH) is a life-threatening condition requiring 
      urgent treatment. There are many different treatment-relevant causes of DAH, 
      making the diagnostic approach to these patients complex and necessitating a 
      multidisciplinary team. We report the case of a kidney transplant recipient in 
      whom all diagnostic efforts did not reveal the cause of DAH, and only autopsy was 
      able to establish an unexpected diagnosis.
