TI  - Pathophysiology of the pleura.
PG  - 121-33
LID - 10.1159/000113629 [doi]
AB  - The pleural mesothelial cell is an essential cell in maintaining the normal 
      homeostasis of the pleural space and it is also a central component of the 
      pathophysiologic processes affecting the pleural space. In this review, we will 
      review the defense mechanisms of the pleural mesothelium and changes in pleural 
      physiology as a result of inflammatory, infectious, and malignant conditions with 
      a focus on cytokine and chemokine networks. We will also review the processes 
      involved in the pathogenesis of pleural fibrosis.
