TI  - Molecular pathology of non-small-cell lung cancer.
PG  - 313-30
AB  - The molecular basis of lung carcinogenesis must be understood more fully and 
      exploited to enhance survival rates of patients suffering from lung cancer. In 
      this review we will discuss the major molecular alterations that occur in lung 
      cancer. Emphasis is placed on alterations that occur early during carcinogenesis 
      since they might be relevant for future screening programs. Finally we will 
      shortly review new approaches that are used to study the molecular pathology of 
      lung cancer and how they can be applied in a clinical setting.
