TI  - Cystic fibrosis diagnosed in an elderly man.
PG  - 98-100
AB  - Although most patients with cystic fibrosis (CF) are diagnosed in early 
      childhood, the diagnosis may be delayed for patients with mild symptoms or 
      single-organ disease. We describe a man with known infertility and a history of 
      productive cough diagnosed with CF at 61 years of age. The patient carries two 
      mutations and one variant in the CF transmembrane conductance regulator gene: 
      394delTT, P99L and R75Q. During a 15-year follow-up time he has developed 
      significant pulmonary disease.
