TI  - A case of congenital pulmonary vein stenosis in an adult.
PG  - 92-4
AB  - A 35-year-old Japanese woman, complaining of dyspnea after her first delivery, 
      was diagnosed as having primary pulmonary hypertension. Continuous intravenous 
      prostacyclin resulted in an improvement in her cardiac function, 6-min walk and 
      New York Heart Association class, before she died of pulmonary hypertension 
      crisis during further evaluation for pulmonary transplantation. Since the autopsy 
      findings revealed that all 4 pulmonary veins were extremely stenotic due to 
      hypoplasia, she was diagnosed as having had congenital pulmonary vein hypoplasia 
      with stenosis.
