TI  - Concurrent left-sided spontaneous pneumothorax in Japanese monogerminal twins.
PG  - 625-7
AB  - Monogerminal twin brothers aged 17 were admitted because of concurrent left-sided 
      spontaneous pneumothorax. A familial background of this common disease in 
      association with the human leukocyte antigen (HLA) has been suggested; however, 
      the actual mode of inheritance in association with HLA typing is still uncertain. 
      HLA analysis in this family revealed the HLA-A24, B61 (40), Cw3, DR4, DR53, and 
      DQ3 haplotype in the twins and their father, who also had a medical history of 
      spontaneous pneumothorax. We report these cases as an extremely rare example of 
      familial occurrence of spontaneous pneumothorax.
