TI  - Essential Image Acquisition Protocols for Thoracic Ultrasonography.
PG  - 231-238
LID - 10.1159/000503585 [doi]
AB  - Image acquisition is the technique of correct placement, holding, and 
      manipulation of the ultrasound probe in an ultrasound examination for the purpose 
      of answering a specific clinical question. We review the literature and discuss 
      the image acquisition protocols used for thoracic ultrasound, explaining, where 
      possible, the associated advantages, disadvantages, and alternatives. A better 
      understanding of how to fine-tune image acquisition specifically for thoracic 
      ultrasound will help physicians on all levels to standardise their practice and 
      improve networking and collaboration. It will also lead to better-quality 
      investigations and, potentially, new applications.
