TI  - Emergency ultrasound of the chest.
PG  - 89-97
LID - 10.1159/000357685 [doi]
AB  - Thoracic ultrasound is a noninvasive and portable diagnostic tool which is highly 
      indicated for an initial workup of thoracic emergencies. The suspicion of a 
      pneumothorax, pneumonia, pulmonary embolism or a lung contusion after trauma can 
      be quickly assessed using ultrasound. Main advantages are its good availability 
      and the steep learning curve. Another advantage of thoracic sonography is that 
      this rapid, symptom-based examination has a high sensitivity and specificity. 
      However, a disadvantage is that only pleura-affecting lesions or lesions visible 
      through a sound window, e.g. an effusion or a subpleural consolidation, can be 
      reached.
