TI  - An unusual endobronchial foreign body: a gauze that migrated from the 
      mediastinum.
PG  - 543-5
AB  - The authors report a 48-year-old white male with lung cancer who was admitted to 
      their clinic with a 1-year history of cough and shortness of breath. The patient 
      was hospitalized because of progression of his complaints over 1 month. On the 
      3rd day of hospitalization, he expectorated a piece of gauze. The authors 
      performed a fiber-optic bronchoscopy and saw pieces of gauze originating from 
      granulation tissue located in the angle of the lower trachea and left main 
      bronchi. A detailed anamnesis revealed that a mediastinoscopy had been performed 
      3 years ago for lung cancer staging: the gauze had migrated from the mediastinum 
      to the endobrochial space.
