TI  - Miliary tuberculosis as a cause of acute empyema.
PG  - 529-32
AB  - Adult respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS) and sepsis are known, life-threatening 
      complications of miliary tuberculosis. This report describes a patient with 
      miliary tuberculosis who rapidly developed an acute tuberculous empyema. She had 
      a fulminant course culminating in ARDS, sepsis and subsequent death. This case 
      highlights the rare association of acute empyema with miliary tuberculosis.
