DP  - 2002
TI  - Increased pleural fluid adenosine deaminase in brucellosis is difficult to 
      differentiate from tuberculosis.
PG  - 556-9
AB  - Pleural involvement in brucellosis is very rare. Current knowledge on brucella 
      pleuritis is limited to a few case studies, and pleural adenosine deaminase (ADA) 
      in brucellosis has not been studied previously. We report the pleural fluid 
      characteristics, including ADA, of two cases with brucella pleurisy. Analysis of 
      the pleural fluids revealed exudative effusions with increased ADA level, 
      decreased glucose concentration, and lymphocyte predominance. The similarity with 
      tuberculous pleurisy was remarkable. We suggest that brucellosis should be 
      considered in the differential diagnosis of tuberculosis, especially in regions 
      endemic for both diseases.
