TI  - Right-to-left atrial shunt without pulmonary artery hypertension.
PG  - 461-3
AB  - A 70-year-old woman without any history of pulmonary or cardiac disease developed 
      breathlessness with severe arterial hypoxemia. Cardiac ultrasound examination and 
      spirometry were normal. Cardiac catheterization and intravenous microbubble 
      injection demonstrated an interatrial right-to-left shunt. The defect was closed 
      surgically, and the patient recovered immediately. On surgery, the aorta was 
      elongated, inducing an angulation of the interatrial septum and leading to the 
      atrial septal defect just above the inferior vena cava.
