TI  - Absence of central microtubules and transposition in the ciliary apparatus of 
      three siblings.
PG  - 449-52
AB  - We studied the cases of three siblings with a history of chronic bronchitis and 
      infertility. The electron-microscopic investigation of the tracheal and bronchial 
      biopsies showed a ciliary defect consisting in the absence of the central 
      microtubules and the transposition of a peripheral doublet. This is a rare and 
      infrequently reported abnormality included in the primary ciliary diskinesia 
      syndrome.
