AB  - Many patients with sarcoidosis suffer from persistent constitutional symptoms 
      such as fatigue and general weakness, even though physiological measures of 
      disease activity returned within normal limits. The following case report 
      demonstrates a sarcoidosis patient with recurring fatigue caused by an 
      obstructive sleep apnea syndrome developed during the course of the disease.
