TI  - Immune Modulation in Asthma: Current Concepts and Future Strategies.
PG  - 566-576
LID - 10.1159/000506651 [doi]
AB  - Asthma treatment concepts have profoundly changed over the last 20 years, from 
      standard therapeutic regimens for all patients with asthma towards individually 
      tailored interventions targeting treatable traits ("precision medicine"). A 
      precise and highly effective immune modulation with minimal adverse effects plays 
      a central role in this new concept. Recently, there have been major advances in 
      the treatment of asthma with immune-modulatory compounds. One example is the 
      approval of several highly potent biologics for the treatment of severe asthma. 
      New immune-modulatory strategies are expected to enter clinical practice in the 
      future; these innovations will be especially important for patients with 
      treatment-resistant asthma.
