DP  - 2019
TI  - Pulmonary Embolism and Gas Exchange.
PG  - 253-262
LID - 10.1159/000501342 [doi]
AB  - Acute pulmonary embolism (PE) impairs hemodynamics, gas exchange, and lung 
      mechanical capacity. Considering PE pathophysiology, most attention has been paid 
      to hemodynamic impairment. However, the most prevalent symptoms in PE patients 
      come from gas exchange alterations, which have not been in the spotlight for many 
      years. Pulmonary physiology and consequent gas exchange impairment play a pivotal 
      role in the high risk of death from PE. In this review, we will look at the 
      pathophysiology of PE, from the vascular occlusion to the resultant heterogeneity 
      in pulmonary perfusion and gas exchange impairment, discussing in detail its 
      causes and consequences.
