TI  - Mesenchymal stem cells as vectors for lung cancer therapy.
PG  - 443-51
LID - 10.1159/000351284 [doi]
AB  - Despite recent advances in treatment, lung cancer accounts for one third of all 
      cancer-related deaths, underlining the need of development of new therapies. 
      Mesenchymal stem cells (MSCs) possess the ability to specifically home into 
      tumours and their metastases. This property of MSCs could be exploited for the 
      delivery of various anti-tumour agents directly into tumours. However, MSCs are 
      not simple delivery vehicles but cells with active physiological process. This 
      review outlines various agents which can be delivered by MSCs with substantial 
      emphasis on TRAIL (tumour necrosis factor-related apoptosis-inducing ligand).
