TI  - Mesothelioma and asbestos-related pleural diseases.
PG  - 1-15
LID - 10.1159/000127577 [doi]
AB  - At present, the use of asbestos is not regulated at a worldwide scale. Moreover, 
      there is a latency period between asbestos exposure and the manifestations of 
      asbestos-related diseases. Consequently, pulmonologists are still dealing with 
      consequences of asbestos exposure, which mainly occur at the pleural surface. The 
      aim of this review is to provide an overview of asbestos-related pleural 
      diseases. We summarized the most relevant data for the diagnosis and the 
      management of benign asbestos pleural effusions, pleural plaques, diffuse pleural 
      thickening and rounded atelectasis. Special attention is dedicated to malignant 
      pleural mesothelioma, given the challenging issues of this disease, the recent 
      advances in its management and the dynamism of research in this area.
