TI  - An unusual cause of T tube obstruction: 'tricho-tracheobezoar'.
PG  - 353-5
AB  - A T tube is an upper airway device well described in the literature which is used 
      to maintain tracheal lumen patency. Although tube occlusion is a known 
      complication, it can be minimized by certain precautions. Otherwise, total 
      occlusion can result in dramatic clinical deterioration or death. Herein, we 
      describe a new clinical entity, 'tricho-tracheobezoar', using a new term defining 
      a hairball in the trachea, which illustrates many of the potential pitfalls in 
      the management of T tubes.
