TI  - Necrotizing granulomata in the lung preceding colonic involvement in 2 patients 
      with Crohn's disease.
PG  - 698-702
AB  - Extraintestinal involvement, including the chest, is common in the late course of 
      Crohn's disease. We describe 2 female patients in whom the course of the disease 
      was unique in two aspects: (1) each had a pulmonary mass with granulomatous 
      inflammation and necrosis, and (2) these findings had preceded the colonic 
      involvement by 5 years. This sequence supports some of the theories on the 
      pathogenesis of Crohn's disease and on its possible relation with sarcoidosis, 
      another idiopathic granulomatous disease.
