TI  - Progressive overlap syndrome due to small cell lung cancer as a paraneoplastic 
      syndrome.
PG  - 588-91
AB  - The association between rheumatic diseases and malignancy has been documented in 
      many studies. Polymyositis and especially dermatomyositis are associated with a 
      higher risk of malignant disease. Furthermore, lung cancer usually develops in 
      patients with a prolonged history of systemic sclerosis accompanied by pulmonary 
      fibrosis. Though overlap syndrome is rarely reported in the associated cancer, 
      this is the first report describing progressive overlap syndrome in small cell 
      lung cancer as a paraneoplastic syndrome.
