DP  - 2005
TI  - Bronchoprotective and bronchodilator effects of an HFA pMDI vs. a CFC pMDI and a 
      DPI containing formoterol in asthma patients.
PG  - 35-7
AB  - In this double-blind, placebo-controlled, crossover study we compared the 
      bronchoprotective effects of formoterol 12 microg inhaled via an HFA-134a inhaler 
      (Modulite HFA) versus a CFC and a DPI device in 38 patients with mild-to-moderate 
      persistent asthma. All three formoterol preparations significantly increased 
      methacholine PD20 and FEV1 and improved small airway function parameters compared 
      with placebo (p < 0.001). No significant differences were observed between 
      formoterol formulations. In conclusion, Modulite HFA formoterol was found to be 
      an effective and well tolerated treatment in patients with asthma, with 
      comparable efficacy to current formoterol preparations.
