TI  - Double aortic arch masquerading as asthma for thirty years.
PG  - 92-5
AB  - A case of a 30-year-old woman with a double-barrelled aorta misdiagnosed as 
      asthma is presented. The patient was significantly improved after surgical 
      treatment but a degree of airway symptoms persisted. She was further investigated 
      and diagnosed with tracheomalacia. The paediatric experience with managing 
      tracheomalacia is briefly reviewed and recommendations for the treatment of the 
      rare adult cases are made. Our report emphasises the importance of early 
      diagnosis and treatment of aortic arch abnormalities.
