TI  - Pergolide-induced dyspnea, bilateral pleural effusion and peripheral edema.
PG  - 580-2
AB  - A patient with severe Parkinson's disease presented with increasing dyspnea, 
      bilateral pleural effusion and peripheral edema that were refractory to diuretic 
      therapy and were first misdiagnosed as signs of right-sided heart failure. 
      Pergolide was the only culprit for this devastating condition and on its 
      discontinuation all signs of fluid retention resolved. In this report, drug 
      reactions to ergots and dopamine agonists are discussed.
